  "question": {
    "text": "Two straight lines having variable slopes <math><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> pass through the fixed points&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> respectively. If <math><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, then the eccentricity of the locus of the point of intersection of the lines is",
    "image": null
  },
